.SH NAME
anpu-advanced - Deeper check — gentle look plus careful tests


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBanpu advanced  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Deeper check — gentle look plus careful tests — runs the advanced profile.

.PP
ADVANCED — safe + polite active. Adds: Subdomains, Takeover, Dirs, Secrets, CORS, Methods, CSRF, Backup, Deps, Active checks (XSS/SQLi/SSRF/blind), exposure pack (ExposedGit, ExposedConfig, Actuator, DebugPages, OAuthAnalyzer, SAMLMetadata, CSWSH, PostMessage, JSSecrets, HiddenParams), technique pack (VerbTamper, CacheDeception, ForbiddenBypass, TakeoverPlus, APIVersion, APIConsole, VHost), vuln-expansion pack (GraphQLFP, GraphQLSchema, SSTIExpand, NoSQLExpand, H2Smuggle adversarial-gated, RedirectPack, LFIPack, CVEPack, CORSPlus, AXFRPlus, BackupPlus, FaviconPlus, DebugMethods, EncodePoly, DiffOracle, Soap, Nsecwalk, Wafdetect, Oauthpack, Ppollute, Swscope, Timeoracle, Jwtconfirm), Katana, Httpx, Subfinder, DNSx, Dalfox, Nuclei.

.PP
Examples:
  anpu advanced https://example.com
  anpu advanced https://example.com --json --output ./reports
  anpu advanced https://example.com --stealth --proxy http://127.0.0.1:8080


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--adversarial\fP[=false]
	enable adversarial hazardous probes — requires --confirm-authorized on authorized ultra targets only; Benign/LowImpact only, no data destruction

.PP
\fB--auto-install\fP[=false]
	auto-install missing external tools mid-scan instead of skipping them

.PP
\fB--budget\fP=0s
	cap total scan wall time, e.g. 15m (0 = uncapped)

.PP
\fB--checkpoint\fP=""
	write per-stage checkpoint snapshots here for --resume

.PP
\fB--confirm-authorized\fP[=false]
	confirm you are authorized to run hazardous adversarial probes against this target (required with --adversarial)

.PP
\fB--csv\fP[=false]
	also write CSV finding export

.PP
\fB--disable\fP=[]
	disable modules (comma-separated, e.g. --disable dirs,active)

.PP
\fB--enable\fP=[]
	enable modules (comma-separated, e.g. --enable portscan,naabu)

.PP
\fB--ghost\fP[=false]
	low-visibility mode for contracted red-team engagements: Chrome 131 JA3, h2, GREASE, Pareto 800-3500ms jitter, no anpu canary substring, proxy rotation, adaptive rate

.PP
\fB--ghost-canary-prefix\fP=""
	custom ghost canary prefix (default "" when --ghost, no anpu substring)

.PP
\fB--ghost-workers\fP=4
	parallel ghost workers for sharded active scanning (0 = sequential)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for advanced

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	also write JSON report

.PP
\fB--jsonl\fP[=false]
	stream findings as JSONL to stdout

.PP
\fB--junit\fP[=false]
	also write JUnit XML export

.PP
\fB--md\fP[=false]
	also write Markdown finding summary

.PP
\fB--only\fP=[]
	run only this module(s) (e.g. --only headers,tls)

.PP
\fB--oob-interactsh\fP[=false]
	use the public interactsh fleet (oast.pro) to CONFIRM blind SSRF/XXE/Log4Shell via observed callbacks

.PP
\fB--output\fP="./reports"
	directory for reports

.PP
\fB--parallel\fP=8
	run snapshot-safe stages concurrently with N workers

.PP
\fB--proxy\fP=""
	proxy URL (http/https/socks5) e.g. http://127.0.0.1:8080

.PP
\fB--proxy-pool\fP=""
	path to file with proxy URLs (one per line, http/https/socks5) for RoundRobin rotation

.PP
\fB--rate-limit\fP=0
